A generic component's slot entries are specialized with the rest of its
contract at each call site, and an insertion of one still carries the entry
the declaration wrote: the splicer finds an entry by pointer among its slot's
declared ones, so an insertion carrying the call site's copy would match none
and render nothing.

`each` binds T to int from `v`, and the population inserts `content` with an
int, which is what the specialized entry accepts. The splice renders the
content `each` wrote for the entry.

deny * `no content` -- the entry is populated, so its fallback is not rendered

-- m.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

component each[T any](v T, item component(content component(x T) node) node) node {
    vbox {
        item() {
            component content(x) {
                text(value="entry content")
            }
        }
    }
}

window {
    var n = 7

    each(v=1) {
        component item(content) {
            content(n) {
                text(value="no content")
            }
        }
    }
}
